            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"><h3>Annotation</h3><table class=\"hl7__eu__lab__report\"><tr><th>Conclusion and Recommendations based on this report and previous findings known to us:</th></tr><tr><td>Thyrotropin (TSH) is slightly elevated above the upper reference limit, which may indicate subclinical or mild hypothyroidism. Clinical correlation is recommended, especially considering the patient's advanced age, as mild TSH elevations can be seen in elderly individuals and may not always require intervention. Further assessment of thyroid function and symptoms is advised.</td></tr></table></div>"
